From 4e095c4b6cd091e7036a44a271c09fdb2a556edf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Gille <mgille@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Dec 2025 14:57:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade Python, Pandas, and SIP versions. Make the builds
 future proof(er).

Python is moved to 3.11 and packaged in Appveyor. This version is a good spot in the lifecycle.

Instead of packaging SIP we generate everything at build time. Will it break in the future?
Almost certainly yes, but when that happens we can pin and fix instead of sticking to some
version, waiting for it to become obsolete and then having lots of pain trying to upgrade.

Simplify and improve the build scripts in general
